//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Dialog
// $Module name: TestCompile.dg
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
//
// Description : Modal dialog that lets the user pick a program (.src) from
//               the currently-selected workspace's [Projects] list and
//               compile it. Shows a busy marquee (an HTML/CSS block in the
//               action strip - see RefreshActionButtons) while compiling and
//               a green/red success/fail message + the .err file
//               contents on failure.
//
//               Compile logic lives in cCompileMixin.pkg (imported by
//               cRefactorApplication). This dialog only handles UI +
//               persistence of the last-picked program per workspace.
//****************************************************************************
Use Windows.pkg
Use cTimer.pkg
Use cFTDeferTimer.pkg
Use cTextEdit.pkg
Use cRefactorCJToolPanel.pkg       // the dock: the RDC Windows library's cRDCCJToolPanel with this program's menu
Use cCJGrid.pkg
Use Cursor.pkg                  // Cursor_Wait/Cursor_Ready around the synchronous Analyze
Use cCJGridColumn.pkg
Use cRDCButton.pkg
Use cRDCForm.pkg
Use cRDCComboForm.pkg
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg  // FT: cFTWebButton - the strip's and the lower row's buttons; cFTWebHtmlBox - the tail, the counts
Use cFTGridHost.pkg             // FT: the two hosts - a grid of 8 px columns (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTPageIsUp.pkg              // FTHostPageIsUp - can the lower row's page take a live push now? (RDCFlexTron)
Use cRDCHeaderGroup.pkg
Use cRefactorApplication.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use cRDCAsyncProcess.pkg
Use cEncodingHelpers.pkg
Use CompileErrorParser.pkg      // ReadCompilerMessages - to gate Analyze on .prn warnings
Use cModAnalyzer.pkg            // PlanFromMessages - StartAutoSelect builds the refactor plan here
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg        // the HTML vocabulary - OpenHtml, IconLabel, the builders
Use FTDashIcons.pkg             // DashIcon - the inline SVG glyphs
Use FTThemeColors.pkg           // FTWebBg / FTCJTheme - the FT palette
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg          // rfOpenOutput / rfCloseOutput - channel file I/O

Open SysFile

Register_Object oSelectFunctionsView

// (The Win32 PBS_MARQUEE/PBM_SETMARQUEE progress-bar retired 2026-07-10: the busy marquee is an
// HTML/CSS block inside the action strip now - it animates on WebView2's own compositor, so it no
// longer freezes whenever the DF thread runs un-pumped, and it needs no dark-theme colour exception.)

// Key prefix used to persist the last-picked program per workspace.
// Full key = CS_LastCompileKeyPrefix + <full path to .sws file>
// Stored under the CS_Settings section in the program's INI.
#IFNDEF CS_LastCompileKeyPrefix
    Define CS_LastCompileKeyPrefix for "LastCompileProgram_"
#ENDIF

// FT: deferred-action selectors for oButtonDeferTimer. An action that activates/realizes another dock,
// pops a modal, or closes/undocks a panel must run off the current stack or it faults (invalid handle,
// err 4410). The flows that start from inside other work - an auto-analyze, the Deep Scan / Tidy Up /
// name-collision offers and the post-plan verify re-scan - arm the 1-ms one-shot timer with one of these,
// and its OnTimer runs the real action natively (mirrors DashboardFT.vw's CI_Dash* + oDeferTimer). The
// bar's buttons armed it too until 2026-09-30; they are framework buttons now (cFTWebButton), whose
// OnButtonClick runs after the click.
/* An Enum_List since 2026-08-10 (Nils), like the board's CI_Chk* selectors: only the first carries
   a number, so adding one is a line with no arithmetic and deleting one leaves no gap to explain.

   Safe to let these renumber - checked, not assumed: piPendingAction on oButtonDeferTimer is only
   ever set from this family, no value is written to the registry, a JSON file or the database, and
   the two files that name them (here and DashboardFT.vw) both do so symbolically. If one is ever
   persisted it stops being an enum member and has to be frozen at its value.

   The #IFNDEF guard stays: this file can be Used more than once, and the guard keys off the first
   member. */
#IFNDEF CI_TCDeferChange
Enum_List
    Define CI_TCDeferChange        for 1  // retained: #IFNDEF guard key (the Change button + top bar were removed)
    Define CI_TCDeferAnalyze              // an auto-analyze -> StartAnalyze (activates the analyzer dock)
    Define CI_TCDeferDeepScan             // the Deep Scan offer's Yes -> Broadcast RunDeepScan (the dashboard owns the scan worker)
    Define CI_TCDeferVerifyScan           // post-plan AUTO verify re-scan -> Broadcast RunDeepScanVerify (no scope confirm)
    Define CI_TCDeferTidyUp               // campaign-exit Tidy Up Yes -> the Folders/Functions view flow (see the OnTimer branch)
    Define CI_TCDeferNameCollision        // return-mismatch nudge Yes -> hand over to the guided view's report runner
End_Enum_List
#ENDIF

Register_Procedure ToggleInformational
Register_Procedure IgnoreSelectedRow
Register_Procedure ClearIgnored
Register_Procedure DoCompileToggle
Register_Procedure SyncWebButtonStates
// Defined in OutputDockFT.dg, which is Used after this file: whether the hidden output dock can be shown as it was.
Register_Function CompileOutputHeld Returns Boolean

// Non-modal, dockable tool panel (was a cRDCModalPanel). Modality was the only thing
// blocking the main editor while errors were shown; as a dock it coexists with the
// Scintilla editor so an error row can jump straight to the source line. Shown via the
// ShowTestCompilePanel entry point at the bottom of this file (not Popup). Docking
// attributes mirror CompilerOutput.dg, the app's other cRefactorCJToolPanel.
Object oTestCompile_dg is a cRefactorCJToolPanel
    // 40 -> 46 units (Nils 2026-09-30, "Grow the dock"): the lower row holds framework buttons too, which need an
    // FT row of 33 px.
    Set Size to 46 530
    Set Location to 193 103
    Set piMinSize to 46 360
    Set peNeighborhood to nhPublic
    /* BOTTOM, always - and set at DESIGN TIME because that is when it is read.
       Create_ToolPanel (cRDCCJToolPanel) passes peBarPosition straight to ComAddDialogBar, so the
       bar is docked wherever the property stood the FIRST time the panel was created. Setting
       it later cannot move an already-docked bar.
       This bar belongs directly above the Compiler Output / Analyzer / Manual Changes tabs, and
       those two are the only bottom bars: CodeJock stacks bottom bars in the order they first
       DOCK, so Test Compile showing before oOutputDock_dg is what puts it on top of them - see
       the note on that ordering in the memory of 2026-07-29, where an auto-restore that realized
       the output dock first inverted the pair for a whole session. (Nils 2026-08-12.) */
    Set peBarPosition to xtpBarBottom
    Set Color to (FTWebBg())
    // Fixed height: the Test Compile bar is a single button/combo row, so resizing it vertically is never
    // meaningful - and with CompilerOutputFT/ModAnalyzerFT stacked below it and the editor above, a drag
    // intended for one of those easily grabs THIS bar by mistake. pbResizable False -> Create_ToolPanel
    // sets the docked cCJDialogBar's ComResizable to False, so it has no resize splitter; the editor and
    // the bottom docks stay resizable.
    Set pbResizable to False

    // Async-compile state:
    // 
    // The compiler runs as a child process launched non-blocking through
    // cRDCAsyncProcess, so the dialog's message pump keeps draining and the
    // UI (elapsed time, live output) stays alive. oCompilePoll_tm polls IsProcessRunning
    // every 100 ms and delegates FinishCompile to the dialog once the
    // child process has exited. psCompilingProgram + pCompilingWS bridge
    // StartCompile - which returns immediately after launching the compile -
    // and FinishCompile, which fires later from the poll timer.

    Property String psCompilingProgram ""
    Property tSwsFile pCompilingWS

    // True once Analyze has been pressed for the current compile output. Reset by StartCompile.
    // LOAD-BEARING again since 2026-07-10: RefreshActionButtons' you-are-here reads it to tell "fresh
    // compile output awaiting Analyze" (light step 2) from "already analyzed" - the grid's
    // pbAnalyzeDataReady alone can't, since it stays True on stale/saved data across a recompile.
    Property Boolean pbAnalyzed False

    // The .sws we've already shown the one-time "compile path exhausted -> Analyze Source?" prompt for this
    // session. Keyed by WORKSPACE identity (like the dashboard's ghsLastAnalyzeWS staleness guard) so the
    // suggestion fires at most once per workspace per session: re-analyzing the same clean output, or a dock
    // re-activation, never re-nags; switching workspaces re-arms it. "" = not yet suggested. (Nils 2026-07-15.)
    Property String psDeepScanSuggestedWS ""

    // --- The campaign-exit latches (Nils 2026-07-19) - see MaybeSuggestTidyUp ---
    // Session-scoped, keyed by workspace identity like psDeepScanSuggestedWS above - deliberately:
    // a latch never outlives the session, so the Tidy Up offer cannot fire off a stale verdict
    // from a previous day (the dashboard's Tidy Up tile stays the always-open door for that case).
    // Each lane records the .sws its LAST verdict declared done, and UN-latches on an opposite
    // verdict; when both point at the current .sws, MaybeSuggestTidyUp pops its one-shot.
    Property String psCompileLaneCleanWS ""   // analyze found nothing actionable (set by NoteCompileLaneVerdict)
    Property String psScanLaneDoneWS     ""   // Deep Scan reported itself exhausted (set by RunDeepScan's verdict)
    Property String psTidyUpSuggestedWS  ""   // the one-shot: Tidy Up already offered for this .sws this session
    Property String psNameCollisionSuggestedWS ""   // the one-shot: name-collision report already offered for this .sws this session
    // The in-scope Explain-row count captured when the compile lane was last found CLEAN (by
    // NoteCompileLaneVerdict, fresh off that analyze). The campaign-exit handoff reads THIS latch rather
    // than the live grid, which a later Deep Scan load would have zeroed by the exhausted moment. > 0 =
    // hand-migration work remains, so the Tidy Up dialog says so instead of claiming "nothing left".
    Property Integer piCompileLaneExplain 0

    // True once a Run Fix Plan has APPLIED inside the scan loop (Deep Scan view). The plan changed the source,
    // so the scan grid is now stale and the natural next step is to Compile + verify the fixes hold - the mirror
    // of the compile path's post-run "recompile to verify". While set, RefreshActionButtons lights Compile (and
    // SyncDeepScanLockdown re-enables the program combo) even though the bar stays in scan mode, so re-scan (the
    // Analyze Source button) is ALSO still available. Cleared when a compile starts (StartCompile) or a fresh scan runs
    // (RunDeepScan). (Nils 2026-07-15 - the deep-scan half of the convergence.)
    Property Boolean pbScanPlanRan False

    // Re-entry guard for StartAnalyze: the analyze pumps the message queue (to animate the
    // marquee + repaint the first-time dock), so a queued/stray Analyze click while it is
    // already running must be ignored. (Was a property on the Analyze button.)
    Property Boolean pbAnalyzing False

    // True while long work is in flight (compile / analyze / plan build): RefreshActionButtons then
    // renders the animated busy marquee at the strip's right edge. Drive it ONLY through
    // SetBusyMarquee (which re-renders the strip); replaced the native oProgress_pb 2026-07-10.
    // Declared up here, before oWebActionBar, with the other state the strip is rendered from.
    Property Boolean pbBusyMarquee False

    // Path to the .prn to analyze when a compile produced NO .err but the listing still has
    // warnings (the clean-build modernization case). Set by FinishCompile ONLY when warnings
    // are actually present; "" otherwise. The Analyze button enables on .err OR this.
    Property String psPrnFilePath ""
    // Full command line (sCmdPath + sCmdArgs) that StartCompile handed to
    // cRDCAsyncProcess. Captured for debugging compiler directives - "what the
    // user thinks they passed" and "what the compiler actually received"
    // diverge often. Not currently displayed; it is the data source for a
    // command-line info-row if the shared dock grows one.
    Property String psCompiledCmdLine ""
    // Absolute path to the temp file that captures the compiler's stdout +
    // stderr, written by the cmd.exe wrapper StartCompile launches. While a
    // df-cli compile runs, UpdateCompileProgress watches it grow and refreshes
    // the live error dock from it. It PERSISTS after the compile (the dock can
    // be reopened to review). Empty when no compile is in flight.
    Property String psCompileLogFile ""

    // The legacy compile's .err path, cached by StartCompile so UpdateCompileProgress can poll it
    // (size-gated) for live error display - the legacy counterpart of psCompileLogFile.
    Property String psLiveErrPath ""
    // The OTHER 32/64-suffix .err candidate: the pre-compile prediction follows the cfg's
    // [Compiler]Platform, but the compiler decides for itself (the authoritative resolve-by-existence
    // only works once the file exists). The live poll watches BOTH and adopts whichever grows.
    Property String psLiveErrPathAlt ""

    // --- Live .prn tail (ALL compilers) ---
    // The growing .prn LISTING is read incrementally while the compiler runs (PollPrnTail, driven by
    // the poll timer) and filtered down to just the diagnostic lines (rfPrnTailConsume). By
    // FinishCompile the messages are in memory: the dock's warning counts and the Analyzer's parse
    // skip their full multi-MB .prn reads (CachedPrn* below). "" = tail disarmed (no compile running,
    // a precompile, or the stale .prn could not be deleted at StartCompile).
    Property String   psLivePrnPath ""
    Property String   psLivePrnPathAlt ""     // the other 32/64-suffix candidate (adopted on growth)
    Property Integer  piPrnTailOffset 0       // bytes consumed so far
    Property UChar[]  pucaPrnTailCarry        // unterminated trailing line, kept as BYTES between reads
    Property Boolean  pbPrnTailUtf8 False     // listing had a UTF-8 BOM (df-cli); else OEM decode
    Property String[] pasPrnTailMsgs          // the harvested diagnostic lines (trimmed, filtered)
    Property Integer  piPrnTailWarn 0
    Property Integer  piPrnTailErr 0
    // How many harvested .prn lines were LAST streamed into the live compiler-output view (legacy compilers
    // only - see UpdateCompileProgress). A no-stdout compiler (DfCompConsole) writes 0 bytes to the redirect
    // log, so its warning-only compile has nothing to tail; this drives the .prn-tail -> live-preview stream
    // instead, refreshing only when the harvest actually grows. Reset to 0 by StartCompile. Nils 2026-07-07.
    Property Integer  piLastPrnStreamCount 0
    // Cache stamp: CachedPrn* only trust the harvest while the on-disk .prn still matches it.
    Property Boolean  pbPrnCacheReady False
    // Background-finalize phase: True while the post-compile tail remainder is still being consumed
    // off the poll timer (see DrainPrnTail / PrnFinalizeTick). Tested FIRST in the timer's OnTimer.
    Property Boolean  pbPrnFinalizing False
    Property String   psPrnCacheFile ""
    Property Integer  piPrnCacheSize 0
    Property DateTime pdtPrnCacheStamp
    // Tick counter incremented every oCompilePoll_tm fire (every 100 ms).
    // Used to sub-sample updates: elapsed-time display every 10 ticks
    // (~1 s), live error-dock refresh every 5 ticks (~500 ms). Reset to 0
    // at the start of each compile.
    Property Integer piCompileTicks 0
    // Re-entrancy latch for UpdateCompileProgress: a tick now does real work (the .err grid refresh +
    // the .prn tail), and the CodeJock grid rebuild is a COM call that can PUMP messages internally -
    // a queued WM_TIMER then re-enters the tick WHILE it is still running, refreshing the grid again
    // -> deeper pumping -> a recursion spiral that freezes the UI and dies on the stack (Nils
    // 2026-07-03: froze at 0:24 into a DF25 LegacyApp compile, then crashed). With the latch, a tick
    // arriving while one is in flight is simply SKIPPED - the next timer fire catches up.
    Property Boolean pbInCompileTick False
    // WALL-CLOCK start of the compile (GetTickCount at StartCompile). The elapsed display and the
    // final "Compiled in Ns" MUST derive from this, not from piCompileTicks / 10: the latch above
    // skips ticks under load, so the tick count undercounts badly (a 24 s compile read "8 s" - Nils
    // 2026-07-03). piCompileTicks remains only as the sub-sampling cadence counter.
    Property Integer piCompileStartTick 0
    // Byte size of psCompileLogFile as of the last tick that refreshed the
    // live error dock. UpdateCompileProgress compares the live file size to
    // this and only refreshes the dock when the log has actually grown -
    // the grid rebuild (and the whole-file read) is the costly part,
    // and most ticks during a single-file compile see no new output. Reset
    // to 0 at the start of each compile.
    Property Integer piLastLogSize 0
    Property Integer piLastErrSize 0
    // Set True by KillCompile right before KillProcess; checked by
    // FinishCompile so the post-mortem can show a "Cancelled" message
    // instead of treating a missing .err file as a clean compile.
    Property Boolean pbCancelled False
    // True from FinishCompile when the compiler did not exit but CRASHED (CompilerCrashWords of its exit
    // code): its listing stops mid-line, so FinalizePrnCache drops the unterminated last line instead of
    // reading it as a diagnostic. Set afresh by every FinishCompile.
    Property Boolean pbCompileCrashed False
    // Full path to the .err file shown on the dialog's bottom row after a
    // failed compile (blank otherwise). The Open button shell-opens this;
    Property String psErrFilePath ""
    // True for a df-cli compile (which streams to stdout): StartCompile then shows the error
    // dock live, UpdateCompileProgress refreshes it as the log grows, and FinishCompile swaps
    // to the parsed .err. Legacy compilers (no streaming) leave it False. Set per-compile.
    Property Boolean pbStreamOutput False
    // Retry budget for the intermittent df-cli "pre-compile needed" bail (external/transient,
    // NOT a code error). FinishCompile retries ONCE immediately when a df-cli compile exits
    // non-zero with NO .err (a genuine compile error would have produced an .err). Reset to 0
    // by the Compile button on a fresh user compile; NOT reset by the retry, so it caps at 1.
    Property Integer piCompileRetries 0

    // Guard so the missing-manifest auto-fix (GenerateProgramManifest + re-compile) is offered AT MOST ONCE
    // per user compile: set when offered, reset to False by the Compile button (like piCompileRetries) so a
    // fresh click may offer again, but the auto re-compile can't loop if the generated manifest doesn't clear
    // the link error.
    Property Boolean pbManifestFixTried False

    // Sibling guard for the "build without a manifest" escape (OfferBuildWithoutManifest): offered AT MOST ONCE
    // per user compile - set when offered, reset by the Compile button - so its auto re-compile can't loop when
    // BuildManifestFile=0 still doesn't clear the link error (a df-cli defect no cfg key can reach).
    Property Boolean pbManifestSkipTried False

    // Sibling guard for the missing-linked-image fix (OfferAndFixMissingLinkImages): offered AT MOST ONCE per
    // user compile - set when offered, reset by the Compile button - so its auto re-compile can't loop when
    // the rewritten .cfg still doesn't link.
    Property Boolean pbLinkImageFixTried False

    // --- df-cli Error 4522: stale PRECOMPILED PACKAGE (.pkd) ---
    // A df-cli compile can bail with "Error 4522: Changes detected in
    // precompiled package , please precompile <PKG>" - it writes NO .err;
    // only the stdout log carries the message (and the package name). A
    // blind retry can never clear it (nothing rebuilds the .pkd), so
    // FinishCompile OFFERS (Yes/No) to run a targeted
    //     df-cli build-file "<AppSrc>\<PKG>" --precompile --workspace "<sws>"
    // (dependency-checked + idempotent). On Yes, a precompile that verifies
    // GREEN (exit 0 AND no package .err) CHAINS straight back into the
    // program compile the user originally requested - the 4522 bail merely
    // interrupted that compile, so resuming it completes the user's own
    // click rather than starting a new build (the YesNo still asks its ONE
    // question). The Studio keeps recompiling a separate manual step, and
    // so did we until 2026-07-19 - live use showed the follow-up press was
    // pure friction: after a green precompile the next action is 100%
    // predictable, and with SEVERAL stale packages the chain collapses
    // Yes/Compile/Yes/Compile into one Yes per package. Every cycle stays
    // gated by its own YesNo, so no unattended loop is possible; a FAILED
    // precompile is terminal (never chained), and psLastPrecompiledPkg
    // guards the chained compile against a same-package re-bail.
    // See TryStartPrecompile / ExtractPrecompilePackage.
    //
    // True while the in-flight child process is a PRECOMPILE rather than the
    // program compile. Read-and-cleared at the top of FinishCompile so a
    // Stop mid-precompile can't leak a stale True into the next compile.
    Property Boolean pbPrecompiling False
    // df-cli's OTHER precompile message ("Warning: Precompiled package X is
    // not compatible, recompiling.") does NOT bail - the package is rebuilt
    // in memory and the compile continues - but the on-disk .pkd is never
    // updated, so the inline recompile repeats on EVERY compile. FinishCompile
    // offers the targeted precompile for it too; when the user answers No,
    // the package name is remembered here so the same question is not asked
    // again every compile (cleared only by program restart - deliberate).
    Property String psDeclinedPrecompilePkg ""
    // Same-package re-bail guard for the auto-chain: the BARE name of the package whose targeted
    // precompile just verified green and chained into the program compile. When THAT chained
    // compile comes back with 4522 (or the variant-2 warning) for the SAME package, the
    // precompile demonstrably did not clear it - re-asking would loop the user through Yes for
    // nothing, so the bail goes terminal-red (and the variant-2 offer is skipped) instead.
    // Cleared by the Compile button (DoCompileToggle): after edits, a fresh user attempt may
    // legitimately hit the same package again. "" = no chain in flight.
    Property String psLastPrecompiledPkg ""
    // Set (to the package's bare name) just before FinishCompile's green-precompile branch chains
    // into StartCompile; read-and-cleared there so the chained compile announces
    // "Precompiled <pkg> - compiling <prog>..." and KEEPS the dock's phase note
    // (psCompileChainNote), while every other compile clears both. "" = not a chained compile.
    Property String psChainedFromPkg ""
    // The stale-.pkd source the user declined to precompile, so the offer is not repeated on every
    // compile. Session-lived and deliberately never cleared by the Compile button (mirrors
    // psDeclinedPrecompilePkg): the file is still stale, and the compiler's own warning stays in the
    // output as the standing reminder.

    // FT: True once the dock's first OnUpdate (initial web realization) has run. Gates the post-activation
    // button re-sync (see OnUpdate) so the very first show - when a WebSet would fault 4402 - is skipped.
    Property Boolean pbFirstUpdateDone False 
    
